[Event "02 · 2.d5 against ...Bc5: avoiding an early f3"]
[Opening "02 · 2.d5 against ...Bc5: avoiding an early f3"]
[Annotator "Potez study notes"]
[Source "https://github.com/lichess-org/chess-openings"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 e5 2. d5 Bc5 3. Nf3 {Develop a piece rather than automatically weakening the king with f3.} d6 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. e4 O-O 6. Be2 c6 7. O-O cxd5 8. exd5 {Plan: Keep the space advantage, but secure the king first. This is an alternative, not proof that 2.d5 must be abandoned.} *

